    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is headlined by **Junior Caminero** (80.95) and **Yordan Alvarez** (79.83), both of whom offer the highest ceilings against favorable matchups. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (4.74 xERA), with park and platoon factors boosting his efficiency well above the baseline. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core play, as his elite 0.452 xwOBA effectively renders the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill level secondary to his high-leverage production potential. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.12) and **Lars Nootbaar** (60.93) round out our top-tier starters, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** receiving a massive 14% lift from a dynamic platoon advantage, justifying his lead-off spot despite a challenging matchup against Logan Webb.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt** (46.22), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Casey Schmitt** carries a decent floor, he was edged out by the superior platoon and order-based efficiency scores of our middle-infield starters like **Caleb Durbin**, whose 52.03 rating is bolstered by a wind-out advantage that the optimizer prioritized over a lower-ceiling bench option. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Gary Sanchez** (42.46) and **Trea Turner** (54.72); the former is struggling against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez\u2019s elite 2.72 xERA, and the latter faces similar headwinds against a tough arm in Harrison. \n\nStrategic risks today center on the high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" statuses. We have aggressively projected **Trea Turner**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Junior Caminero**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Kyle Schwarber** into their typical slots, but any mid-afternoon lineup shifts could force us to re-evaluate these efficiency scores. Specifically, **Dillon Dingler** remains benched (37.65) not just due to efficiency, but because he falls below our 40.0 absolute floor requirement; he, along with **Jacob Gonzalez** (38.92), will be held in reserve to preserve our valuable game caps for a more favorable slate.",
